LEGJSON {"kind": "dash", "argv": ["/data/local/tmp/s29q3_0190/kpy/wheel", "dash", "/data/local/tmp/s29q3_0190/N4.litertlm", "gpu", "/data/local/tmp/s29q3_0190/long-context-1024-gen256.txt"], "pid": 3673, "start_epoch": 1793252404.0482132, "iterations": [{"init_total_ms": 24476.05, "ttft_s": 3.1715624995000002, "prefill_tokens": 1338, "prefill_tok_s": 429.10641582706995, "decode_tokens": 256, "decode_tok_s": 18.707378250744537, "turns": {"prefill": [{"tokens": 1338, "tokens_per_s": 429.10641582706995}, {"tokens": 2, "tokens_per_s": 4.970970303925473}], "decode": [{"tokens": 256, "tokens_per_s": 18.707378250744537}]}, "turn_used": "turn 1 of each kind", "wall_s": 17.22}, {"init_total_ms": 24475.79, "ttft_s": 3.2469257089999997, "prefill_tokens": 1338, "prefill_tok_s": 418.95187103731826, "decode_tokens": 256, "decode_tok_s": 18.7823619367069, "turns": {"prefill": [{"tokens": 1338, "tokens_per_s": 418.95187103731826}, {"tokens": 2, "tokens_per_s": 4.629694938335542}], "decode": [{"tokens": 256, "tokens_per_s": 18.7823619367069}]}, "turn_used": "turn 1 of each kind", "wall_s": 17.27}], "replies": [{"text": "", "channels": {"thought": "Okay, the user wants a list of 25 distinct things that on-device AI can do on a phone that a cloud model can't. Let me start by recalling what on-device AI entails. It's processing data locally, not sending it to the cloud. So the key points are local processing, no internet, privacy, lower latency, etc.\n\nFirst, I need to think of tasks that require real-time processing without internet. For example, real-time language translation. On-device AI can translate text instantly without connecting to a server. That's one. Then, maybe things like voice commands for navigation. If the phone can process voice commands locally, it doesn't need a cloud connection.\n\nAnother could be image recognition. If the phone can recognize objects in real-time without sending the image to the cloud, that's a benefit. Also, privacy is a big one. Local processing means user data isn't sent to the cloud, so that's a privacy aspect.\n\nWhat about predictive text? On-device AI can learn from the user's typing habits and predict the next word, which is faster and more private. Then, maybe things like augmented reality features that don't require an internet connection. Like AR filters that run locally.\n\nAlso, things like local machine learning models"}}, {"text": "", "channels": {"thought": "Okay, the user wants a list of 25 distinct things that on-device AI can do on a phone that a cloud model can't. Let me start by recalling what on-device AI entails. It's processing data locally, not sending it to the cloud. So the key points are local processing, no internet, privacy, lower latency, etc.\n\nFirst, I need to think of tasks that require real-time processing without internet. For example, real-time language translation. On-device AI can translate text instantly without connecting to a server. That's one. Then, maybe things like voice commands for navigation. If the phone can process voice commands locally, it doesn't need a cloud connection.\n\nAnother could be image recognition. If the phone can recognize objects in real-time without sending the image to the cloud, that's a benefit. Also, privacy is a big one. Local processing means user data isn't sent to the cloud, so that's a privacy aspect.\n\nWhat about predictive text? On-device AI can learn from the user's typing habits and predict the next word, which is faster and more private. Then, maybe things like augmented reality features that don't require an internet connection. Like AR filters that run locally.\n\nAlso, things like local machine learning models"}}], "versions": {"python": "3.14.8", "platform": "android", "machine": "aarch64", "litert-lm-api": "0.19.0"}, "lib": {"path": "/data/local/tmp/s29q3_0190/kpy/wheel/litert_lm/liblitert-lm.so", "bytes": 22656360, "sha256": "28fa8433febc49a99f4bd3ef8cb82c2912457cfe274d97944debeabdeb97fc78"}, "litert_lm_file": "/data